White Paper Fragment

The Personal Reasoning Corpus (PRC)

Abstract

Today’s AI models possess broad capabilities but only transient context.

Humans possess continuity but limited bandwidth.

A Personal Reasoning Corpus (PRC) sits between them.

It is neither the model nor merely a notebook.

It is an executable cognitive substrate that preserves:

* abstractions,
* operators,
* preferences,
* tests,
* examples,
* failures,
* terminology,
* and developmental history.

The PRC is owned by the individual.

The AI is the current interpreter.

Different interpreters may come and go.

The corpus persists.

