The Oscillation Principle

Good reasoning alternates between two modes.

Compress
↓
Expand
↓
Compress
↓
Expand

Compression discovers structure.

Expansion tests structure.

Neither alone is sufficient.

Mathematically,

K_{t+1}
=
E(C(K_t))

where

* C compresses
* E expands through examples

Repeated oscillation gradually improves both representation and understanding.

